From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mrmikedrum <mrmikedrum@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:58:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Restore counters and damage on cards a snapshot reuses

GameSnapshot.restore reuses cards that still exist and copies only some of their state, so counters
and damage added after the snapshot survived the restore. Copy both back with the rest.

Goldfish-Upstream: offer

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/GameSnapshot.java | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/GameSnapshot.java b/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/GameSnapshot.java
index 2d64547a..fa41e1be 100644
--- a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/GameSnapshot.java
+++ b/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/GameSnapshot.java
@@ -492,6 +492,9 @@ public class GameSnapshot {
         newCard.setGameTimestamp(fromCard.getGameTimestamp());
         newCard.setLayerTimestamp(fromCard.getLayerTimestamp());
         newCard.setTapped(fromCard.isTapped());
+        // A card that still exists is reused on restore, so its counters and damage must be put back too.
+        newCard.setCounters(HashMultiset.create(fromCard.getCounters()));
+        newCard.setDamage(fromCard.getDamage());
         newCard.setFaceDown(fromCard.isFaceDown());
         newCard.setManifested(fromCard.getManifestedSA());
         newCard.setSickness(fromCard.hasSickness());
